fig(doc,'figure5_features','Figure 5. Feature discovery at two adjusted-p thresholds.','Side-by-side bars give total treatment-associated ASVs at q ≤ 0.05 and q ≤ 0.25. The latter totals include the former; bars are not stacked. Counts are 5/34, 14/43, and 1/3 for 16S, ITS, and 18S, respectively. Models are management-only and exploratory; full coefficients and uncertainty fields are in the supplementary data.')
fig(doc,'figure6_networks','Figure 6. Descriptive network topology by management.','Connected ASVs, mean degree, and density for the three marker datasets and cross-marker graph. Green denotes NT and orange till. Each bar summarizes one inferred graph; graph-construction and sampling limitations are described in Methods. The large AMF mean-degree contrast contracted from 6.69 versus 42.54 to a balanced NT median of 36.34 versus 42.54 for till (Table S7).')
fig(doc,'figure7_sensitivity','Figure 7. Community-test sensitivity to balanced subsampling.','Each point is one of 20 overlapping balanced subsets. Boxes show interquartile ranges and black medians; whiskers extend to the most extreme values within 1.5 interquartile ranges. Left: PERMANOVA R²; right: p values, with a dashed 0.05 threshold. Group sizes are 11/11, 10/10, 10/10, and 9/9 for 16S, ITS, 18S, and cross-marker analyses. Detection counts are 18/20, 7/20, 4/20, and 20/20. These are descriptive sensitivity frequencies, not independent replications or power estimates; date and site confounding persist.')
fig(doc,'figure8_carbon','Figure 8. Sequential carbon-inclusive community models.','Cells display sequential R² (%) and unadjusted p values for management, C after management, and management × C after both main terms. These models do not estimate a carbon-adjusted management effect. Date, site, and depth are omitted; C units and analytical fraction remain unverified, and AMF chemistry is unresolved. Table 6 gives numeric results. The ITS carbon-overlay graph is retained in the existing supplementary atlas (Figure S31).')
